# OneKhusa push payment API: raw requests for the VS Code REST Client or Visual Studio .http editor.
# Fill in the variables below. Never commit real credentials.

@baseUrl = https://api.onekhusa.com/sandbox/v1
@apiKey = your-api-key
@apiSecret = your-api-secret
@organisationId = your-organisation-id
@merchantAccountNumber = 12345678

### 1. Get an access token (valid for 5 minutes)
# @name token
POST {{baseUrl}}/account/getAccessToken
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{
  "apiKey": "{{apiKey}}",
  "apiSecret": "{{apiSecret}}",
  "organisationId": "{{organisationId}}",
  "merchantAccountNumber": {{merchantAccountNumber}}
}

### 2. List connectors; use a mobile money (channelCode "M") connectorId below
GET {{baseUrl}}/core/connectors/GetAll
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 3. Initiate a direct push payment (sends a PIN prompt to the customer's phone)
# Sandbox test wallets: Airtel Money 221100000101, TNM Mpamba 231100000101 (PIN 1234).
# Use the connectorId of the matching provider.
# A 200 with responseCode "I100" only means the prompt was sent. Wait for the webhook.
POST {{baseUrl}}/collections/push/direct/initiate
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en
X-Idempotency-Key: {{$guid}}

{
  "merchantAccountNumber": {{merchantAccountNumber}},
  "connectorId": 550044,
  "payerAccountNumber": "221100000101",
  "sourceReferenceNumber": "PPHTTP{{$timestamp}}",
  "transactionDescription": "Sample order payment",
  "transactionAmount": 100,
  "capturedBy": "you@example.com"
}

### 4. Deliver a webhook to the local sample app
# The signature must be the lowercase hex HMAC-SHA512 of the exact body below, keyed with the
# pushpayment.success secret. Compute it with:
#   printf '%s' '<body on one line>' | openssl dgst -sha512 -hmac '<secret>'
# The app's Webhook simulator page does this for you.
POST http://localhost:5085/webhooks/onekhusa/pushpayment
Content-Type: application/json
X-OneKhusa-Webhook-Event: pushpayment.success
X-OneKhusa-Webhook-Signature: paste-computed-signature-here

{"connectorId":550044,"merchantReferenceNumber":"PPHTTP123","transactionStatusCode":"S","transactionAmount":100}
